592186120198 1068 #edb/ref 17592186301864 13194139533413 17592186045585 true] [17592186120198 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045487 13194139533413 17592186045585 true] [17592186120198 1071 "If $h(x) = \\sqrt{2x + 3}$, find $(h^{-1})^{′}(x)$ as a function of $h^{-1}(x)$." 13194139533413 17592186045585 false] [17592186120198 1071 "If $h(x)=\\sqrt{2x+3},$ find ${({h}^{-1})}^{′}(x)$ as a function of ${h}^{-1}(x).$" 13194139533413 17592186045585 true] [17592186120198 1074 "**Step 1:** First, we write the inverse function implicitly. The given function is $y=\\sqrt{2x+3},$ and to write the inverse function implicitly, we swap $x$ and $y$ as follows:\n\n$$\nx=\\sqrt{2y+3}\n$$\n\nNote that in the equation above, we have $y={h}^{-1}(x).$\n\n**Step 2:** Next, we differentiate. The overall goal is to find $\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x},$ but the equation is already solved for $x,$ so we compute $\\frac{\\text{d}x}{\\text{d}y}$ and then take the reciprocal:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{\\text{d}x}{\\text{d}y} & =\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}y}[\\sqrt{2y+3}] \\\\ \\frac{\\text{d}x}{\\text{d}y} & =\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}y}[(2y+3)^{1/2}] \\\\ \\frac{\\text{d}x}{\\text{d}y} & =(2y+3)^{-1/2} \\\\ \\frac{\\text{d}x}{\\text{d}y} & =\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{2y+3}} \\\\ \\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x} & =\\sqrt{2y+3}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n**Step 3:** Lastly, we write the result in terms of ${h}^{-1}(x).$ Since $y={h}^{-1}(x),$ we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}[{h}^{-1}(x)] & =\\sqrt{2{h}^{-1}(x)+3} \\\\ {({h}^{-1})}^{′}(x) & =\\sqrt{2{h}^{-1}(x)+3}.\\end{aligned}\n$$" 13194139533413 17592186045585 true] [17592186120201 1068 #edb/ref 17592186117337 13194139533413 17592186045585 false] [17592186120201 1068 #edb/ref 17592186301415 13194139533413 17592186045585 true] [17592186120201 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045487 13194139533413 17592186045585 true] [17592186120201 1071 "If $x = 2\\sqrt{y} - \\frac{3}{\\sqrt{y}}$, find $\\frac{dy}{dx}$ at the point $(5, 9)$." 13194139533413 17592186045585 false] [17592186120201 1071 "If $x=2\\sqrt{y}-\\frac{3}{\\sqrt{y}},$ find $\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}$ at the point $(5,9).$" 13194139533413 17592186045585 true] [17592186120201 1074 "First, we differentiate $x(y)$ with respect to $y:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{\\text{d}x}{\\text{d}y} & =\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}y}(2\\sqrt{y}-\\frac{3}{\\sqrt{y}}) \\\\  & =2\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}y}(\\sqrt{y})-3\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}y}(\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{y}}) \\\\  & =2\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}y}({y}^{1/2})-3\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}y}({y}^{-1/2}) \\\\  & =2\\cdot \\frac{1}{2}{y}^{-1/2}-3\\cdot (-\\frac{1}{2}{y}^{-3/2}) \\\\  & ={y}^{-1/2}+\\frac{3}{2}{y}^{-3/2} \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{y}}+\\frac{3}{2\\sqrt{{y}^{3}}} \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{y}}+\\frac{3}{2y\\sqrt{y}} \\\\  & =\\frac{2y+3}{2y\\sqrt{y}}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, taking the reciprocal of $\\frac{\\text{d}x}{\\text{d}y},$ we get\n\n$$\n\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}={(\\frac{\\text{d}x}{\\text{d}y})}^{-1}=\\frac{2y\\sqrt{y}}{2y+3}.\n$$\n\nFinally, substituting the point $(5,9),$ we find\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}{|}_{(x,y)=(5,9)} & =\\frac{2(9)\\sqrt{9}}{2(9)+3}=\\frac{18}{7}.\\end{aligned}\n$$" 13194139533413 17592186045585 true] [17592186120202 1068 #edb/ref 17592186117343 13194139533413 17592186045585 false] [17592186120202 1068 #edb/ref 17592186301366 13194139533413 17592186045585 true] [17592186120202 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045487 13194139533413 17592186045585 true] [17592186120202 1071 "Given a curve $x = \\frac{2}{3}y^{3} - y^{2}$, what is the equation of the tangent to the curve at the point $(9, 3)$?" 13194139533413 17592186045585 false] [17592186120202 1071 "Given a curve $x=\\frac{2}{3}{y}^{3}-{y}^{2},$ what is the equation of the tangent to the curve at the point $(9,3)?$" 13194139533413 17592186045585 true] [17592186120202 1074 "First, we differentiate $x(y)$ with respect to $y:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{\\text{d}x}{\\text{d}y} & =\\frac{\\tex