uation and squaring, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}y & =\\sqrt{8}\\operatorname{tan}⁡t \\\\ \\frac{y}{\\sqrt{8}} & =\\operatorname{tan}⁡t \\\\ \\frac{{y}^{2}}{(\\sqrt{8})^{2}} & ={tan}^{2}⁡t \\\\ \\frac{{y}^{2}}{8} & ={tan}^{2}⁡t.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSubstituting the two equations into the identity ${tan}^{2}⁡t+1={sec}^{2}⁡t$ and rearranging, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{tan}^{2}⁡t+1 & ={sec}^{2}⁡t \\\\ \\frac{{y}^{2}}{8}+1 & =\\frac{{x}^{2}}{25} \\\\ \\frac{{x}^{2}}{25}-\\frac{{y}^{2}}{8} & =1.\\end{aligned}\n$$" 13194139533413 17592186045585 true] [17592186302249 1068 #edb/ref 17592186301588 13194139533413 17592186045585 true] [17592186302249 1069 "q-325938" 13194139533413 17592186045585 true] [17592186302249 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045485 13194139533413 17592186045585 true] [17592186302249 1071 "Find the Cartesian equation of the hyperbola $x=4\\operatorname{sec}⁡t,\\,y=7\\operatorname{tan}⁡t.$\n\n{{field-1}}\n$=1$" 13194139533413 17592186045585 true] [17592186302249 1072 #uuid "14757807-d472-5c26-8560-91938e110338" 13194139533413 17592186045585 true] [17592186302249 1074 "To find the Cartesian equation of the hyperbola, we need to eliminate the parameter $t.$ We can do this using the secant-tangent identity.\n\n- Isolating the $\\operatorname{sec}⁡t$ term in the $x$-equation and squaring, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}x & =4\\operatorname{sec}⁡t \\\\ \\frac{x}{4} & =\\operatorname{sec}⁡t \\\\ \\frac{{x}^{2}}{{4}^{2}} & ={sec}^{2}⁡t \\\\ \\frac{{x}^{2}}{16} & ={sec}^{2}⁡t.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n- Isolating the $\\operatorname{tan}⁡t$ term in the $y$-equation and squaring, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}y & =7\\operatorname{tan}⁡t \\\\ \\frac{y}{7} & =\\operatorname{tan}⁡t \\\\ \\frac{{y}^{2}}{{7}^{2}} & ={tan}^{2}⁡t \\\\ \\frac{{y}^{2}}{49} & ={tan}^{2}⁡t.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSubstituting the two equations into the identity ${tan}^{2}⁡t+1={sec}^{2}⁡t$ and rearranging, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{tan}^{2}⁡t+1 & ={sec}^{2}⁡t \\\\ \\frac{{y}^{2}}{49}+1 & =\\frac{