72 #uuid "718e7839-05f5-5267-b703-e30edd06aa60" 13194139533413 17592186045585 true] [17592186302438 1074 "We will find the general solution to the equation, and then generate all of the solutions in the required domain.\n\nThe general solution to our equation is given by\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}4x-\\frac{\\pi }{3} & =\\frac{\\pi }{3}+n\\pi .\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSolving our equation for $x,$ we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}4x & =\\frac{\\pi }{3}+\\frac{\\pi }{3}+n\\pi  \\\\ 4x & =\\frac{2\\pi }{3}+n\\pi  \\\\ x & =\\frac{\\pi }{6}+\\frac{n\\pi }{4} \\\\ x & =\\frac{(3n+2)\\pi }{12}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nWe set $n=0,\\pm 1,\\pm 2,…,$ until we have generated all solutions in the domain $0\\le x<2\\pi .$\n\n- Setting $n=0$ gives $x=\\frac{\\pi }{6}$\n\n- Setting $n=1$ gives $x=\\frac{5\\pi }{12}$\n\n- Setting $n=2$ gives $x=\\frac{2\\pi }{3}$\n\n- Setting $n=3$ gives $x=\\frac{11\\pi }{12}$\n\n- Setting $n=4$ gives $x=\\frac{7\\pi }{6}$\n\n- Setting $n=5$ gives $x=\\frac{17\\pi }{12}$\n\n- Setting $n=6$ gives $x=\\frac{5\\pi }{3}$\n\n- Setting $n=7$ gives $x=\\frac{23\\pi }{12}$\n\nAll other values of $n$ generate solutions outside the domain $0\\le x<2\\pi .$ \n\nSo, the solutions to the equation, in ascending order, are \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{x}_{1} & =\\frac{\\pi }{6},\\,{x}_{2}=\\frac{5\\pi }{12},\\,{x}_{3}=\\frac{2\\pi }{3},\\,{x}_{4}=\\frac{11\\pi }{12}, \\\\ {x}_{5} & =\\frac{7\\pi }{6},\\,{x}_{6}=\\frac{17\\pi }{12},\\,{x}_{7}=\\frac{5\\pi }{3},\\,{x}_{8}=\\frac{23\\pi }{12}.\\end{aligned}\n$$" 13194139533413 17592186045585 true] [17592186302439 1068 #edb/ref 17592186301410 13194139533413 17592186045585 true] [17592186302439 1068 #edb/ref 17592186301472 13194139533413 17592186045585 true] [17592186302439 1068 #edb/ref 17592186301532 13194139533413 17592186045585 true] [17592186302439 1068 #edb/ref 17592186301658 13194139533413 17592186045585 true] [17592186302439 1069 "q-328366" 13194139533413 17592186045585 true] [17592186302439 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045485 13194139533413 17592186045585 true] [17592186302439 1071 "Expressed in **ascending order** in radians, the **exact solutions** to the equation  $\\operatorname{tan}⁡(2x)=-1,$ for $-\\pi \\le x<\\pi ,$  are\n\n${x}_{1}=$\n{{field-1}}$,\\,{x}_{2}=$\n{{field-2}}$,\\,{x}_{3}=$\n{{field-3}}$,\\,{x}_{4}=$\n{{field-4}}." 13194139533413 17592186045585 true] [17592186302439 1072 #uuid "0417656a-bd25-5f25-9b77-af16b473f382" 13194139533413 17592186045585 true] [17592186302439 1074 "We will find the general solution to the equation, and then generate all of the solutions in the required domain.\n\nThe general solution to our equation is given by\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}2x & =-\\frac{\\pi }{4}+n\\pi .\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSolving our equation for $x,$ we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}x & =-\\frac{\\pi }{8}+\\frac{n\\pi }{2} \\\\ x & =\\frac{(4n-1)\\pi }{8}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nWe set $n=0,\\pm 1,\\pm 2,…,$ until we have generated all solutions in the domain $-\\pi \\le x<\\pi .$\n\n- Setting $n=-1$ gives $x=-\\frac{5\\pi }{8}$\n\n- Setting $n=0$ gives $x=-\\frac{\\pi }{8}$\n\n- Setting $n=1$ gives $x=\\frac{3\\pi }{8}$\n\n- Setting $n=2$ gives $x=\\frac{7\\pi }{8}$\n\nAll other values of $n$ generate solutions outside the domain $-\\pi \\le x<\\pi .$ \n\nSo, in ascending order,  the solutions are \n\n$$\n{x}_{1}=-\\frac{5\\pi }{8},\\,{x}_{2}=-\\frac{\\pi }{8},\\,{x}_{3}=\\frac{3\\pi }{8},\\,{x}_{4}=\\frac{7\\pi }{8}\n$$" 13194139533413 17592186045585 true] [17592186302440 1068 #edb/ref 17592186301344 13194139533413 17592186045585 true] [17592186302440 1068 #edb/ref 17592186301645 13194139533413 17592186045585 true] [17592186302440 1069 "q-328369" 13194139533413 17592186045585 true] [17592186302440 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045487 13194139533413 17592186045585 true] [17592186302440 1071 "Expressed in **ascending order** in degrees, the **exact solutions** to the equation $\\operatorname{tan}⁡(2x+{45}^{∘})=1,$ for $-{180}^{∘}\\le x<0,$  are\n\n${x}_{1}=$\n{{field-1}}${}^{∘},\\,{x}_{2}=$\n{{field-2}}${}^{∘}.$" 13194139533413 17592186045585 true] [17592186302440 1072 #uuid "a29f8975-533d-56ce-8412-c1ce4e2952d2" 13194139533413 17592186045585 true] [17592186302440 1074 "We will find the general solution to the equation, and then generate all of the solutions in the required domain.\n\nThe general solution to our equation is given by\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}2x+{45}^{∘} & ={45}^{∘}+n\\cdot {180}^{∘}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSolving our equation for $x,$ we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}2x & =-{45}^{∘}+{45}^{∘}+n\\cdot {180}^{∘} \\\\ 2x & =n\\cdot {180}^{∘} \\\\ x & =n\\cdot {90}^{∘}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nWe set $n=0,\\pm 1,\\pm 2,…,$ until we have generated all solutions in the domain $-{180}^{∘}\\le x<0.$\n\n- Setting $n=-2$ gives $x=-{180}^{∘}$\n\n- Setting $n=-1$ gives $x=-{90}^{∘}$\n\nAll other values of $n$ generate solutions outside the domain $-{180}^{∘}\\le x<0.$ \n\nSo, the solutions to the equation, in ascending order, are \n\n$$\n{x}_{1}={-180}^{∘},\\,{x}_{2}={-90}^{∘}.\n$$" 13194139533413 17592186045585 true] [17592186302441 1068 #edb/ref 17592186301912 13194139533413 17592186045585 true] [17592186302441 1069 "q-32837" 13194139533413 17592186045585 true] [17592186302441 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045487 13194139533413 17592186045585 true] [17592186302441 1071 "Given $f(t)=({t}^{3}-1)\\,i+({t}^{2}-2)\\,j+4{t}^{2}\\,k$, evaluate $({f}^{′}\\cdot f)^{′}(0).$" 13194139533413 17592186045585 true] [17592186302441 1072 #uuid "829808f0-e345-5eeb-99ad-5982ddad6fb7" 13194139533413 17592186045585 true] [17592186302441 1074 "Using the dot product rule, we can write:\n\n$$\n({f}^{′}\\cdot f)^{′}(t)={f}^{″}(t)\\cdot f(t)+{f}^{′}(t)\\cdot {f}^{′}(t)\n$$\n\nLet's now find the first and second derivative of the function.\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{f}^{′}(t) & =\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}({t}^{3}-1)\\,i+\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}({t}^{2}-2)\\,j+\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}(4{t}^{2})\\,k \\\\  & =3{t}^{2}\\,i+2t\\,j+4\\cdot 2t\\,k \\\\  & =3{t}^{2}\\,i+2t\\,j+8t\\,k \\\\ {f}^{″}(t) & =\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}(3{t}^{2})\\,i+\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}(2t)\\,j+\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}(8t)\\,k \\\\  & =3\\cdot 2t\\,i+2j+8\\,k \\\\  & =6t\\,i+2j+8\\,k\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, we obtain:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}({f}^{′}\\cdot f)^{′}(0) & ={f}^{″}(0)\\cdot f(0)+{f}^{′}(0)\\cdot {f}^{′}(0) \\\\  & =(6(0)\\,i+2\\,j+8\\,k)\\cdot (({0}^{3}-1)\\,i+({0}^{2}-2)\\,j+4(0)^{2}\\,k)+(3(0)^{2}\\,i+2(0)\\,j+8(0)\\,k)\\cdot (3(0)^{2}\\,i+2(0)\\,j+8(0)\\,k) \\\\  & =(2\\,j+8\\,k)\\cdot (-i-2\\,j) \\\\  & =0(-1)+2(-2)+(0) \\\\  & =-4\\end{aligned}\n$$" 13194139533413 17592186045585 true] [17592186302442 1068 #edb/ref 17592186301340 13194139533413 17592186045585 true] [17592186302442 1068 #edb/ref 17592186301527 13194139533413 17592186045585 true] [17592186302442 1069 "q-328374" 13194139533413 17592186045585 true] [17592186302442 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045487 13194139533413 17592186045585 true] [17592186302442 1071 "The center of the hyperbola $6{x}^{2}-{y}^{2}-24x+10y=7$ is$\\,\\,($\n{{field-1}}$,$\n{{field-2}}\n$).$" 13194139533413 17592186045585 true] [17592186302442 1072 #uuid "2d46bedb-abf3-5e0e-be7c-58482d588bb6" 13194139533413 17592186045585 true] [17592186302442 1074 "The equation of a horizontal hyperbola centered at $(h,k)$ is given by\n\n$$\n\\frac{(x-h)^{2}}{{a}^{2}}-\\frac{(y-k)^{2}}{{b}^{2}}=1.\n$$\n\nTo rewrite the given equation in standard form, group the $x$ and $y$ terms and complete the squares:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}6{x}^{2}-{y}^{2}-24x+10y & =7 \\\\ 6({x}^{2}-4x)-({y}^{2}-10y) & =7 \\\\ 6[(x-2)^{2}-4]-[(y-5)^{2}-25] & =7 \\\\ 6(x-2)^{2}-24-(y-5)^{2}+25 & =7 \\\\ 6(x-2)^{2}-(y-5)^{2} & =7+24-25 \\\\ 6(x-2)^{2}-(y-5)^{2} & =6 \\\\ \\frac{(x-2)^{2}}{1}-\\frac{(y-5)^{2}}{6}=1.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nHence, the center of the hyperbola is $(\\,2,5\\,).$" 13194139533413 17592186045585 true] [17592186302443 1068 #edb/ref 17592186301453 13194139533413 17592186045585 true] [17592186302443 1068 #edb/ref 17592186301782 13194139533413 17592186045585 true] [17592186302443 1069 "q-328382" 13194139533413 17592186045585 true] [17592186302443 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045487 13194139533413 17592186045585 true] [17592186302443 1071 "The center of the hyperbola ${x}^{2}-9{y}^{2}-6x-36y=54$ is$\\,\\,($\n{{field-1}}$,$\n{{field-2}}\n$).$" 13194139533413 17592186045585 true] [17592186302443 1072 #uuid "6bc48671-a72b-5e74-a845-63b61e701b90" 13194139533413 17592186045585 true] [17592186302443 1074 "The equation of a horizontal hyperbola centered at $(h,k)$ is given by\n\n$$\n\\frac{(x-h)^{2}}{{a}^{2}}-\\frac{(y-k)^{2}}{{b}^{2}}=1.\n$$\n\nTo rewrite the equation of the hyperbola in standard form, we need to group $x$ and $y$ terms and complete the squares as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{x}^{2}-9{y}^{2}-6x-36y & =54 \\\\ {x}^{2}-6x-9{y}^{2}-36y & =54 \\\\ [{x}^{2}-6x]-9[{y}^{2}+4y] & =54 \\\\ [(x-3)^{2}-9]-9[(y+2)^{2}-4] & =54 \\\\ (x-3)^{2}-9-9(y+2)^{2}+36 & =54 \\\\ (x-3)^{2}-9(y+2)^{2} & =54+9-36 \\\\ (x-3)^{2}-9(y+2)^{2} & =27 \\\\ \\frac{(x-3)^{2}}{(\\sqrt{27})^{2}}-\\frac{(y+2)^{2}}{(\\sqrt{3})^{2}} & =1 \\\\ \\frac{(x-3)^{2}}{(\\sqrt{27})^{2}}-\\frac{(y-(-2))^{2}}{(\\sqrt{3})^{2}} & =1\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nHence, the center of the hyperbola is $(\\,3,-2\\,).$" 13194139533413 17592186045585 true] [17592186302444 1068 #edb/ref 17592186301579 13194139533413 17592186045585 true] [17592186302444 1068 #edb/ref 17592186301583 13194139533413 17592186045585 true] [17592186302444 1069 "q-328391" 13194139533413 17592186045585 true] [17592186302444 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045487 13194139533413 17592186045585 true] [17592186302444 1071 "The center of the hyperbola $9{y}^{2}-{x}^{2}+54y+10x=-20$ is$\\,\\,($\n{{field-1}}$,$\n{{field-2}}\n$).$" 13194139533413 17592186045585 true] [17592186302444 1072 #uuid "87c1b0c8-82c8-58bc-9817-885965b84893" 13194139533413 17592186045585 true] [17592186302444 1074 "The equation of a vertical hyperbola centered at $(h,k)$ is given by\n\n$$\n\\frac{(y-k)^{2}}{{a}^{2}}-\\frac{(x-h)^{2}}{{b}^{2}}=1.\n$$\n\nTo rewrite the equation of the hyperbola in the above form, we need to group $x$ and $y$ terms and complete the squares, as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}9{y}^{2}-{x}^{2}+54y+10x & =-20 \\\\ 9{y}^{2}+54y-{x}^{2}+10x & =-20 \\\\ 9[{y}^{2}+6y]-[{x}^{2}-10x] & =-20 \\\\ 9[(y+3)^{2}-9]-[(x-5)^{2}-25] & =-20 \\\\ 9(y+3)^{2}-81-(x-5)^{2}+25 & =-20 \\\\ 9(y+3)^{2}-(x-5)^{2} & =-20+81-25 \\\\ 9(y+3)^{2}-(x-5)^{2} & =36 \\\\ \\frac{(y+3)^{2}}{4}-\\frac{(x-5)^{2}}{36} & =1 \\\\ \\frac{(y-(-3))^{2}}{4}-\\frac{(x-5)^{2}}{36} & =1\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nHence, the center of the hyperbola is $(\\,5,-3\\,).$" 13194139533413 17592186045585 true] [17592186302445 1068 #edb/ref 17592186301295 13194139533413 17592186045585 true] [17592186302445 1068 #edb/ref 17592186301388 13194139533413 17592186045585 true] [17592186302445 1069 "q-328392" 13194139533413 17592186045585 true] [17592186302445 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045487 13194139533413 17592186045585 true] [17592186302445 1071 "The center of the hyperbola $-{x}^{2}+16{y}^{2}-32y-8x=16$ is$\\,\\,($\n{{field-1}}$,$\n{{field-2}}\n$).$" 13194139533413 17592186045585 true] [17592186302445 1072 #uuid "e24c2ffc-0e54-5b21-812d-3a6dbc07b16e" 13194139533413 17592186045585 true] [17592186302445 1074 "The equation of a vertical hyperbola centered at $(h,k)$ is given by\n\n$$\n\\frac{(y-k)^{2}}{{a}^{2}}-\\frac{(x-h)^{2}}{{b}^{2}}=1.\n$$\n\nTo rewrite the equation of the hyperbola in the above form, we need to group $x$ and $y$ terms and complete the squares, as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}-{x}^{2}+16{y}^{2}-32y-8x & =16 \\\\ 16{y}^{2}-32y-{x}^{2}-8x & =16 \\\\ 16[{y}^{2}-2y]-[{x}^{2}+8x] & =16 \\\\ 16[(y-1)^{2}-1]-[(x+4)^{2}-16] & =16 \\\\ 16(y-1)^{2}-16-(x+4)^{2}+16 & =16 \\\\ 16(y-1)^{2}-(x+4)^{2} & =16 \\\\ \\frac{(y-1)^{2}}{1}-\\frac{(x+4)^{2}}{16} & =1 \\\\ \\frac{(y-1)^{2}}{1}-\\frac{(x-(-4))^{2}}{16} & =1\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nHence, the center of the hyperbola is $(\\,-4,1\\,).$" 13194139533413 17592186045585 true] [17592186302446 1068 #edb/ref 17592186301259 13194139533413 17592186045585 true] [17592186302446 1068 #edb/ref 17592186301721 13194139533413 17592186045585 true] [17592186302446 1069 "q-328393" 13194139533413 17592186045585 true] [17592186302446 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045485 13194139533413 17592186045585 true] [17592186302446 1071 "Expressed in **ascending order** in radians, the exact solutions to the equation  $\\operatorname{sin}⁡x=\\frac{\\sqrt{3}}{2},$ for $0\\le x<2\\pi ,$ are\n\n$x=$ \n{{field-1}}$,\\,x=$\n{{field-2}}." 13194139533413 17592186045585 true] [17592186302446 1072 #uuid "b4e34b2f-1c92-5f18-a0cc-db49cea0c12e" 13194139533413 17592186045585 true] [17592186302446 1074 "First, we find the principal value:\n\n$$\nx=arcsin\\,(\\frac{\\sqrt{3}}{2})=\\frac{\\pi }{3}\n$$\n\nSince $\\frac{\\pi }{3}$ lies inside the required domain, our first solution is ${x}_{1}=\\frac{\\pi }{3}.$\n\nOur first solution lies in the first quadrant and has a reference angle of ${\\theta }_{R}=\\frac{\\pi }{3}.$ Since $\\operatorname{sin}⁡x>0,$ the second solution must lie in the second quadrant, and it also has a reference angle ${\\theta }_{R}=\\frac{\\pi }{3}.$\n\n![](images/d5/d50a4a9f62be8b8af4cc657a5b0ab1547288b844eaa05af1a57ed39b8afa0d6d.png)\n\nSince the second solution ${x}_{2}$ lies in the $2$nd quadrant, we can find it using the reference angle as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{x}_{2} & =\\pi -{\\theta }_{R} \\\\  & =\\pi -\\frac{\\pi }{3} \\\\  & =\\frac{2\\pi }{3}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo, the solutions to the equation, in ascending order, are \n\n$$\nx=\\frac{\\pi }{3},\\,x=\\frac{2\\pi }{3}.\n$$" 13194139533413 17592186045585 true] [17592186302447 1068 #edb/ref 17592186301590 13194139533413 17592186045585 true] [17592186302447 1068 #edb/ref 17592186301786 13194139533413 17592186045585 true] [17592186302447 1069 "q-328394" 13194139533413 17592186045585 true] [17592186302447 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045487 13194139533413 17592186045585 true] [17592186302447 1071 "The center of the hyperbola $9{y}^{2}-{x}^{2}+36y+10x=25$ is$\\,\\,($\n{{field-1}}$,$\n{{field-2}}\n$).$" 13194139533413 17592186045585 true] [17592186302447 1072 #uuid "ac92697b-85e7-535c-a80b-31f9bab4329b" 13194139533413 17592186045585 true] [17592186302447 1074 "The equation of a vertical hyperbola centered at $(h,k)$ is given by\n\n$$\n\\frac{(y-k)^{2}}{{a}^{2}}-\\frac{(x-h)^{2}}{{b}^{2}}=1.\n$$\n\nTo rewrite the equation of the hyperbola in the above form, we need to group $x$ and $y$ terms and complete the squares, as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}9{y}^{2}-{x}^{2}+36y+10x & =25 \\\\ 9{y}^{2}+36y-{x}^{2}+10x & =25 \\\\ 9[{y}^{2}+4y]-[{x}^{2}-10x] & =25 \\\\ 9[(y+2)^{2}-4]-[(x-5)^{2}-25] & =25 \\\\ 9(y+2)^{2}-36-(x-5)^{2}+25 & =25 \\\\ 9(y+2)^{2}-(x-5)^{2} & =25+36-25 \\\\ 9(y+2)^{2}-(x-5)^{2} & =36 \\\\ \\frac{(y+2)^{2}}{4}-\\frac{(x-5)^{2}}{36} & =1 \\\\ \\frac{(y-(-2))^{2}}{4}-\\frac{(x-5)^{2}}{36} & =1\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nHence, the center is $(\\,5,-2\\,).$" 13194139533413 17592186045585 true] [17592186302448 1068 #edb/ref 17592186301339 13194139533413 17592186045585 true] [17592186302448 1068 #edb/ref 17592186301807 13194139533413 17592186045585 true] [17592186302448 1069 "q-328397" 13194139533413 17592186045585 true] [17592186302448 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045487 13194139533413 17592186045585 true] [17592186302448 1071 "The center of the hyperbola ${y}^{2}-4{x}^{2}-6y+8x=-1$ is$\\,\\,($\n{{field-1}}$,$\n{{field-2}}\n$).$" 13194139533413 17592186045585 true] [17592186302448 1072 #uuid "95f0d924-de91-5f95-a0e5-29279698cfa6" 13194139533413 17592186045585 true] [17592186302448 1074 "The equation of a vertical hyperbola centered at $(h,k)$ is given by\n\n$$\n\\frac{(y-k)^{2}}{{a}^{2}}-\\frac{(x-h)^{2}}{{b}^{2}}=1.\n$$\n\nTo rewrite the equation of the hyperbola in the above form, we need to group $x$ and $y$ terms and complete the squares, as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{y}^{2}-4{x}^{2}-6y+8x & =-1 \\\\ {y}^{2}-6y-4{x}^{2}+8x & =-1 \\\\ [{y}^{2}-6y]-4[{x}^{2}-2x] & =-1 \\\\ [(y-3)^{2}-9]-4[(x-1)^{2}-1] & =-1 \\\\ (y-3)^{2}-9-4(x-1)^{2}+4 & =-1 \\\\ (y-3)^{2}-4(x-1)^{2} & =-1+9-4 \\\\ (y-3)^{2}-4(x-1)^{2} & =4 \\\\ \\frac{(y-3)^{2}}{{2}^{2}}-\\frac{(x-1)^{2}}{{1}^{2}} & =1\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nHence, the center of the hyperbola is $(\\,1,3\\,).$" 13194139533413 17592186045585 true] [17592186302449 1068 #edb/ref 17592186301347 13194139533413 17592186045585 true] [17592186302449 1068 #edb/ref 17592186301350 13194139533413 17592186045585 true] [17592186302449 1069 "q-328400" 13194139533413 17592186045585 true] [17592186302449 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045487 13194139533413 17592186045585 true] [17592186302449 1071 "The center of the hyperbola $-16{x}^{2}+{y}^{2}-8y+32x=16$ is$\\,\\,($\n{{field-1}}$,$\n{{field-2}}\n$).$" 13194139533413 17592186045585 true] [17592186302449 1072 #uuid "d48e3bc5-46c6-5a06-aa22-627c6b9e6983" 13194139533413 17592186045585 true] [17592186302449 1074 "The equation of a vertical hyperbola centered at $(h,k)$ is given by\n\n$$\n\\frac{(y-k)^{2}}{{a}^{2}}-\\frac{(x-h)^{2}}{{b}^{2}}=1.\n$$\n\nTo rewrite the equation of the hyperbola in the above form, we need to group $x$ and $y$ terms and complete the squares, as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}-16{x}^{2}+{y}^{2}-8y+32x=16 \\\\ {y}^{2}-8y\\,-\\,16{x}^{2}+32x & =16 \\\\ [{y}^{2}-8y]\\,-\\,16[{x}^{2}-2x] & =16 \\\\ [(y-4)^{2}-16]\\,-\\,16\\,[(x-1)^{2}-1] & =16 \\\\ (y-4)^{2}-16\\,-\\,16(x-1)^{2}+16 & =16 \\\\ (y-4)^{2}-16(x-1)^{2} & =16 \\\\ \\frac{(y-4)^{2}}{16}-\\frac{(x-1)^{2}}{1} & =1 \\\\ \\frac{(y-4)^{2}}{{4}^{2}}-\\frac{(x-1)^{2}}{{1}^{2}} & =1\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nHence, the center of the hyperbola is $(\\,1,4\\,).$" 13194139533413 17592186045585 true] [17592186302450 1068 #edb/ref 17592186301280 13194139533413 17592186045585 true] [17592186302450 1068 #edb/ref 17592186301479 13194139533413 17592186045585 true] [17592186302450 1069 "q-328401" 13194139533413 17592186045585 true] [17592186302450 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045487 13194139533413 17592186045585 true] [17592186302450 1071 "The center of the hyperbola $16{y}^{2}-25{x}^{2}+96y=256$ is$\\,\\,($\n{{field-1}}$,$\n{{field-2}}\n$).$" 13194139533413 17592186045585 true] [17592186302450 1072 #uuid "937b8770-6fd6-5e2a-a6a3-e0d265d81c6d" 13194139533413 17592186045585 true] [17592186302450 1074 "The equation of a vertical hyperbola centered at $(h,k)$ is given by\n\n$$\n\\frac{(y-k)^{2}}{{a}^{2}}-\\frac{(x-h)^{2}}{{b}^{2}}=1.\n$$\n\nTo rewrite the equation of the hyperbola in the above form, we need to group $x$ and $y$ terms and complete the squares, as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}16{y}^{2}-25{x}^{2}+96y & =256 \\\\ 16{y}^{2}+96y\\,-\\,25{x}^{2} & =256 \\\\ 16[{y}^{2}+6y]\\,-\\,25{x}^{2} & =256 \\\\ 16[(y+3)^{2}-9]\\,-\\,25{x}^{2} & =256 \\\\ 16(y+3)^{2}-144\\,-\\,25{x}^{2} & =256 \\\\ 16(y+3)^{2}-25{x}^{2} & =256+144 \\\\ 16(y+3)^{2}-25{x}^{2} & =400 \\\\ \\frac{(y+3)^{2}}{25}-\\frac{{x}^{2}}{16} & =1 \\\\ \\frac{(y-(-3))^{2}}{25}-\\frac{{x}^{2}}{16} & =1\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nHence, the center of the hyperbola is $(\\,0,-3\\,).$" 13194139533413 17592186045585 true] [17592186302451 1068 #edb/ref 17592186301311 13194139533413 17592186045585 true] [17592186302451 1068 #edb/ref 17592186301615 13194139533413 17592186045585 true] [17592186302451 1069 "q-328402" 13194139533413 17592186045585 true] [17592186302451 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045487 13194139533413 17592186045585 true] [17592186302451 1071 "The center of the hyperbola ${y}^{2}-4{x}^{2}+40x=136$ is$\\,\\,($\n{{field-1}}$,$\n{{field-2}}\n$).$" 13194139533413 17592186045585 true] [17592186302451 1072 #uuid "e9bf578a-e50f-5940-a73e-9bb2f570f83a" 13194139533413 17592186045585 true] [17592186302451 1074 "The equation of a vertical hyperbola centered at $(h,k)$ is given by\n\n$$\n\\frac{(y-k)^{2}}{{a}^{2}}-\\frac{(x-h)^{2}}{{b}^{2}}=1.\n$$\n\nTo rewrite the equation of the hyperbola in the above form, we need to group $x$ and $y$ terms and complete the squares, as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{y}^{2}-4{x}^{2}+40x & =136 \\\\ {y}^{2}\\,-\\,4{x}^{2}+40x & =136 \\\\ {y}^{2}\\,-\\,4[{x}^{2}-10x] & =136 \\\\ {y}^{2}\\,-\\,4\\,[(x-5)^{2}-25] & =136 \\\\ {y}^{2}-4(x-5)^{2}+100 & =136 \\\\ {y}^{2}-4(x-5)^{2} & =36 \\\\ \\frac{(y-0)^{2}}{36}-\\frac{(x-5)^{2}}{9} & =1\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nHence, the center of the hyperbola is $(\\,5,0\\,).$" 13194139533413 17592186045585 true] [17592186302452 1068 #edb/ref 17592186301319 13194139533413 17592186045585 true] [17592186302452 1068 #edb/ref 17592186301810 13194139533413 17592186045585 true] [17592186302452 1069 "q-328403" 13194139533413 17592186045585 true] [17592186302452 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045487 13194139533413 17592186045585 true] [17592186302452 1071 "The center of the hyperbola $9{y}^{2}-16{x}^{2}-72y=-108$ is$\\,\\,($\n{{field-1}}$,$\n{{field-2}}\n$).$" 13194139533413 17592186045585 true] [17592186302452 1072 #uuid "71af2021-2901-5409-b275-c9e044fe1d83" 13194139533413 17592186045585 true] [17592186302452 1074 "The equation of a vertical hyperbola centered at $(h,k)$ is given by\n\n$$\n\\frac{(y-k)^{2}}{{a}^{2}}-\\frac{(x-h)^{2}}{{b}^{2}}=1.\n$$\n\nTo rewrite the equation of the hyperbola in the above form, we need to group $x$ and $y$ terms and complete the squares, as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}9{y}^{2}-16{x}^{2}-72y & =-108 \\\\ 9{y}^{2}-72y-16{x}^{2} & =-108 \\\\ 9[{y}^{2}-8y]-16[{x}^{2}] & =-108 \\\\ 9[(y-4)^{2}-16]-16{x}^{2} & =-108 \\\\ 9(y-4)^{2}-144-16{x}^{2} & =-108 \\\\ 9(y-4)^{2}-16{x}^{2} & =-108+144 \\\\ 9(y-4)^{2}-16{x}^{2} & =36 \\\\ \\frac{(y-4)^{2}}{4}-\\frac{{x}^{2}}{9/4} & =1\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nHence, the center of the hyperbola is $(\\,0,4\\,).$" 13194139533413 17592186045585 true]] :edb/tempids {"answer-006c6611-e018-504a-a01c-32aef354674d" 17592186299939 "answer-011fae4e-c40e-5543-bf07-c0c1656584a7" 17592186299940 "answer-01c168f8-05c3-5f43-ac97-03fa4301d749" 17592186299941 "answer-01e2124c-250c-5553-90ac-ad036367a54c" 17592186299942 "answer-01f65e8b-4617-531e-b590-48e7cae4c340" 17592186299943 "answer-01